<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The above FR have been reviewed by the ACM and approved by the BoD at their respective meetings held on Jan 29,25. The SA have carried out limited review of these FR.   2. The Cooperates only in one segment, namely, manufacture and marketing of components for the transportation industry.   3. Exceptional items (net) represents the following:   (i) Provision for Customer Quality Claims:       (a) An amt of INR 5.68Cr for the nine months ended Dec 31, 2024 (INR 0.61Cr for the Q E Dec 31, 2024; INR 5.07Cr for the half year ended Sep 30,2024) has been provided for claims related to defective valves supplied to a domestic customer. The Company has initiated an insurance claim, which is currently under process, and will recognize the recovery once there is virtual certainty of realization. Mgmt believes the provision made is sufficient to cover the estimated liability.       (b) An amt of INR 4.13Cr was provided for the year ended Mar31, 2024 for claims relating to defective valves supplied to two overseas customers (INR 1.13Cr for the nine months ended Dec 31,2023 for one of the overseas customers). For one such customer, an income of INR 4.25Cr was recognized in the nine months ended Dec 31,2024, representing the insurance claim receivable for product liability after receipt of the final survey report. Additionally, during the QE Sep30,2024 and nine months ended Dec 31,2024, the excess provision of INR 0.76 Cr was reversed.   (ii) Merger-related Exp:        INR 0.10 Cr for the QE Dec 31, 2024; INR 0.12 Cr for the nine months ended Dec 31, 2024; INR 0.02 Cr for the QE Sep 30, 2024; and INR 1.20 Cr for the year ended Mar31, 2024.   (iii) Vol Retirement Exp:         INR 0.09Cr for the nine months ended Dec 31, 2023 and for the year ended Mar 31, 2024.   4. During the current qtr, the Company had opted for the lower corporate tax rate available u/s 115BAA of the Income Tax Act,1961 (IT) effective from FY 2023-24. Consequent to the above, the Company has reversed the MAT Credit recognised under deferred tax asset relating to FY 23-24 of Rs.3.66Cr (with corresponding reversal of provision for tax under MAT of equivalent amount) and MAT Credit relating to earlier years amounting to Rs.2.27Cr. Further, the Company has also remeasured its net deferred tax assets, on account of adoption of sec.115BAA of the IT Act, resulting in an impact of Rs. 8.27 Cr for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31, 2024. The tax cost recognised for the qtr also includes impact of reversal of MAT Credit recognised for the half year ended Sep 30, 2024 under deferred tax of Rs. 2.73Cr with corresponding reversal of provision for tax under MAT of equivalent amt under current tax.   5. The BoD of the Company in their meeting held on Feb 09,2024, considered and approved the proposed scheme of amalgamation (“Scheme”) of the Company and RBL with and into RML with effect from Apr 01, 2024 (‘the appointed date’) u/s 230 to 232 of the CA, 2013, and other applicable Sec and provisions of the said Act read together with the rules made thereunder. BSE Ltd &amp; NSE Ltd vide their respective letters dated Jul 18, 2024 have issued no adverse observation/ no objection to the scheme. Further, the scheme has been approved by Share. Hol and Crds through their meetings held on Nov 20, 2024 &amp; Nov 21,2024 respectively. The aforesaid scheme is subject to the approval of NCLT and such other approvals as may be required.   6. The previous period figures have been re-grouped wherever necessary to conform to current period's presentation.   7.  There are no subs/Assoc/JV company(ies) and hence only Standalone financials are provided.   8. The FR for the qtr and nine months ended Dec 31, 2024 are being published in the newspaper as per the format prescribed under Reg.33 of SEBI (LODR), 2015. The FR are also available on the SE web: www.bseindia.com and www.nseindia.com and on the company's web- www.ranegroup.com.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
